      "math_academy_id": "e-977",
      "problem": "To which quadrant does the point $(4,-2)$ belong?",
      "worked_solution": "In order to identify the quadrant to which the point $(4,-2)$ belongs, we start by plotting the point.\n\n- The $x$-coordinate of the point is $4,$ so we move $4$ units to the right of the origin.\n\n- The $y$-coordinate of the point is $-2,$ so we move $2$ units down from the origin.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/02b0dd5d2d125277ffb6fc637fa612eef451c06522efa7655d8374c68641e796.png)\n\nBased on the graph, we can tell that the point belongs to quadrant $\\textrm{IV}$,  the fourth quadrant.",
